          <y:NodeLabel alignment="center" autoSizePolicy="content" fontFamily="Gill Sans" fontSize="15" fontStyle="plain" hasBackgroundColor="false" hasLineColor="false" height="229.00157356262207" horizontalTextPosition="center" iconTextGap="4" modelName="custom" textColor="#000000" verticalTextPosition="bottom" visible="true" width="344.8625793457031" x="28.03066684888762" xml:space="preserve" y="26.879729849646537">Words
====

A Frame is displayed.

A display is a render step and a refresh step.

The rendering is done in three steps.
* The view hierarchy is layouted.
* The views are animated.
* The view hierarchy is drawn into a framebuffer.

The refresh is done in two steps.
* The offscreen framebuffer is used to refresh the screen 
* (Optionally) the screen framebuffers are swapped
